  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.9,
      "end_seconds": 2.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Welcome. Make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 7.15,
      "end_seconds": 10.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Morning, doctor, sorry about the rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.67,
      "end_seconds": 14.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "How are things, what's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.29,
      "end_seconds": 19.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "Um, so... no symptoms. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.42,
      "end_seconds": 24.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "how troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.12,
      "end_seconds": 35.13,
      "duration_seconds": 9.01,
      "text": "Okay, so about a five out of ten. Slightly tired was there, but it's gone away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.8,
      "end_seconds": 42.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "have you had no symptoms before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.74,
      "end_seconds": 54.25,
      "duration_seconds": 7.51,
      "text": "sorry, what was I saying, I had a similar thing last winter. It went away"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.08,
      "end_seconds": 59.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "And what about black stools, weight loss or heavy periods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.29,
      "end_seconds": 64.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "No, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.79,
      "end_seconds": 68.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Has there been any blood in the stool?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.03,
      "end_seconds": 77.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "yeah, not at all, no blood in the stool"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.12,
      "end_seconds": 80.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.33,
      "end_seconds": 84.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "yeah, no, joints are fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.89,
      "end_seconds": 98.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "let's run through your medicines"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.41,
      "end_seconds": 113.69,
      "duration_seconds": 14.28,
      "text": "Sodium valproate, 500 milligrams, twice a day. Ibuprofen. I take it 400 milligrams, most days. I'd been on lamotrigine, not any more though, I stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.91,
      "end_seconds": 118.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.81,
      "end_seconds": 123.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "I have epilepsy, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.24,
      "end_seconds": 137.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.73,
      "end_seconds": 152.34,
      "duration_seconds": 12.61,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. Not much, I mostly stay in these days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.9,
      "end_seconds": 155.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.93,
      "end_seconds": 159.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Yeah, no allergies at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.48,
      "end_seconds": 162.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Let me take your readings now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.54,
      "end_seconds": 178.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Okay, nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.24,
      "end_seconds": 205.45,
      "duration_seconds": 9.21,
      "text": "okay: heart rate 84, BP is 112 over 72, SpO2 97 percent on room air and temp 36.5 degrees"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.84,
      "end_seconds": 209.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.74,
      "end_seconds": 211.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.48,
      "end_seconds": 215.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.78,
      "end_seconds": 234.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.71,
      "text": "Your pulse and blood pressure are normal, and the eyelids are pale."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.8,
      "end_seconds": 242.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.39,
      "end_seconds": 274.18,
      "duration_seconds": 12.79,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, it points towards iron-deficiency anaemia needing a source found. It could also be a bowel cancer, so so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.55,
      "end_seconds": 282.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Okay, so is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.82,
      "end_seconds": 302.32,
      "duration_seconds": 19.5,
      "text": "I understand the worry at the moment I'd say it's iron-deficiency anaemia needing a source found, and we'll know more once the a camera test of the stomach and bowel is back so, to recap quickly you've had no symptoms, and no blood in the stool or weight loss"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.93,
      "end_seconds": 305.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "That's it, you know, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.88,
      "end_seconds": 313.62,
      "duration_seconds": 6.74,
      "text": "I think a camera test of the stomach and bowel makes sense here, for iron-deficiency anaemia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.67,
      "end_seconds": 315.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "right, understood"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.87,
      "end_seconds": 344.55,
      "duration_seconds": 26.68,
      "text": "I think an iron study makes sense here, for anaemia. Let's get a coeliac blood test, for anaemia. What I'm giving you is ferrous sulfate, 200 milligrams, once a day, three months. That's for iron deficiency. Stop the ibuprofen and we will refer you for scopes. Book a review after the tests. Alright, that's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 346.3,
      "end_seconds": 348.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Well, thank you, that's helpful."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.77,
      "end_seconds": 351.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "goodbye for now"
    }
  ]
}